## Transformation Objectives

Execute a comprehensive project transformation to achieve the following outcomes:

**Code Quality Standards:**
- Eliminate all dead code, unused imports, and unreachable statements
- Remove component duplication and consolidate overlapping functionality
- Refactor all code smells including excessive complexity, magic numbers, and anti-patterns
- Ensure all functions, components, and modules have single, clear responsibilities
- Apply consistent naming conventions throughout the codebase

**Architecture Integration:**
- Verify all module imports and exports are correctly wired and functional
- Ensure no orphaned components, utilities, or services exist
- Confirm all epics and stories connect through defined architectural patterns
- Validate end-to-end integration of all features from user input to persistence
- Check that state management flows correctly between Zustand stores and Dexie.js persistence

**Testing and Validation:**
- All existing tests must pass without modification to test logic
- Fix only syntax errors and genuine implementation bugs in test files
- Tests must reflect real-world use cases and edge conditions
- Achieve incremental test coverage improvements across all modules
- Maintain test coverage thresholds defined in validation gate specifications

**Acceptance Criteria Compliance:**
- Trace every implemented feature to its corresponding acceptance criteria
- Verify all story requirements are demonstrably satisfied
- Confirm all demo checkpoints are functional and documented
- Ensure user acceptance criteria map to actual implemented behavior

**Documentation Alignment:**
- Update all documentation to reflect actual implementation details
- Ensure dev notes match current code structure and behavior
- Align retrospective findings with current code state
- Complete any missing documentation for recently implemented features

## Execution Constraints

**Resource Management:**
- Execute only one background task at any given time
- Kill all terminal processes before starting new tasks
- Kill all terminal processes after completing tasks
- Monitor memory and CPU usage during long-running operations

**Migration Strategy:**
- Preserve all existing functionality during refactoring
- Apply migration patterns for any removed or replaced code
- Maintain backward compatibility where required
- Document all breaking changes with migration paths

